Objective

Implement a complete production-ready subscription paywall for the QGuard Messaging application that works seamlessly across both Android and Desktop platforms using a single user account.

The subscription system must synchronize in real time so that a user's subscription status is automatically recognized regardless of which platform they use.

===========================================================
USER FLOW
===========================================================

New User

1. Install QGuard Messaging.
2. Register a new account.
3. Verify email (if enabled).
4. Login.
5. Check subscription status.
6. If no active subscription exists:
   - Redirect the user to the Subscription page.
   - Prevent access to all messaging features.
   - Allow only the Pricing, Profile, and Subscription pages.
7. The user must purchase the STARTER Plan using either:
   - Google Play Billing (Android)
   - PayPal
8. After successful payment:
   - Verify the payment on the backend.
   - Create or update the user's subscription.
   - Activate the STARTER plan.
   - Unlock the application automatically.
9. Redirect the user to the main dashboard.

===========================================================
EXISTING USER FLOW
===========================================================

When an existing subscriber logs in:

1. Authenticate user.
2. Retrieve subscription status from the backend.
3. If STARTER subscription is Active:
   - Skip the paywall.
   - Grant full access immediately.
4. If Expired:
   - Redirect to Subscription page.
5. If Cancelled:
   - Redirect to Subscription page.
6. If Payment Failed:
   - Redirect to Subscription page.
7. If Trial Expired:
   - Redirect to Subscription page.

===========================================================
CROSS-PLATFORM SUBSCRIPTION SYNCHRONIZATION
===========================================================

A subscription belongs to the user's account, NOT to the device.

Example:

Android Purchase

↓

User Account

↓

Backend Database

↓

Subscription Active

↓

Desktop Login

↓

Desktop immediately recognizes:

✓ Active STARTER Plan
✓ Remaining subscription period
✓ Subscription expiration
✓ Subscription ID
✓ Customer ID

The Desktop application must NOT ask the user to purchase again if their account already has an active subscription.

Likewise:

Desktop Purchase

↓

Backend

↓

Android Login

↓

Automatically unlock Android application.

